A set named by both an enclosing group directive and a spec directive inside it is
a duplicate: the group already joins X to build, so restating //plumb:build on the
spec is rejected. This is the same duplicate-directive rule as repeating a directive on
one declaration, now applied across the group/spec boundary. (A spec directive
naming a *different* set is still unioned in; see group_and_spec_directive_union.)
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrDuplicateDirective
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

type A struct{}

//plumb:build
var (
	//plumb:build
	X = A{}
)
